---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LabPlayground from '../../components/LabPlayground';
---

<Layout
  title="The Lab · Interactive Robotics & Systems Experiments"
  description="Playful and experimental projects: 2D kinematics simulation, PID tuning, and software playgrounds."
>
  <div class="lab-page section-spacing">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="lab-header">
        <span class="chapter-num">/lab · Playground & Experiments</span>
        <h1>Interactive Systems Lab</h1>
        <p class="narrative-lead" style="max-width: 720px; margin-top: 0.75rem;">
          Engineering ideas made tangible. A sandbox for differential kinematics, control theory gains, microcontroller circuit design, and unconventional software experiments.
        </p>
      </header>

      {/* Main Interactive Experiment: 2D Differential Drive & PID */}
      <LabPlayground client:load />

      {/* Second Lab Experiment: Hardware Pinout & Circuit Workbench */}
      <section class="hardware-workbench-section" style="margin-top: 5rem;">
        <div class="asym-grid asym-grid-57">
          <div>
            <span class="mono-tag" style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Experiment 02 / Hardware Bridge</span>
            <h2>Jetson Orin Nano to ESP32 Serial Interface</h2>
            <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.65;">
              In mobile robotics, high-level path planning (Nav2) runs on a Linux SBC, while real-time motor PWM must execute on a deterministic microcontroller. This hardware bridge handles bidirectional serial communications:
            </p>

            <ul style="margin: 1.25rem 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; font-size: 0.9375rem; color: var(--text-muted); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem;">
              <li><strong>Linux Side:</strong> Custom Python serial publisher streaming normalized wheel ticks over <code>/dev/ttyUSB0</code> at 115200 baud.</li>
              <li><strong>ESP32 Side:</strong> FreeRTOS dual-core tasks: Core 0 computes PID wheel speeds; Core 1 samples quadrature encoders.</li>
              <li><strong>Safety Interlock:</strong> Auto-brakes within 250ms if UART serial keep-alive times out.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="surface-card font-mono" style="font-size: 0.75rem; background-color: var(--bg-surface);">
            <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-light); padding-bottom: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
              <span style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-main);">UART Packet Protocol Frame</span>
              <span style="color: var(--accent-orange);">CRC-8 Protected</span>
            </div>

            <pre style="background: var(--bg-primary); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto; color: var(--text-main); line-height: 1.5;">
[BYTE 0] 0xAA (Start of Frame Header)
[BYTE 1] 0x55 (Sync Marker)
[BYTE 2] Left Wheel Target Velocity (int16_t, m/s * 1000)
[BYTE 4] Right Wheel Target Velocity (int16_t, m/s * 1000)
[BYTE 6] Watchdog Sequence Counter (uint8_t)
[BYTE 7] CRC-8 Checksum (Dallas/Maxim 1-Wire polynomial)
            </pre>

            <div style="margin-top: 1rem; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; color: var(--text-faint);">
              <span>Sample Rate: 50Hz</span>
              <span>Baud: 115,200</span>
              <span style="color: #10B981;">Latency: ~1.2ms</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      {/* Experimental Archives */}
      <section style="margin-top: 5rem;">
        <span class="chapter-num">Archived Playgrounds</span>
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Front-End & Creative Experiments</h3>

        <div class="asym-grid asym-grid-half">
          <div class="surface-card">
            <span class="mono-tag" style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">UI Experiment</span>
            <h4>Code Flow: Typography & Elevation Sandbox</h4>
            <p style="font-size: 0.875rem; margin-top: 0.35rem;">
              Experimental layout engine exploring extreme asymmetric editorial column flow and responsive font scaling without media query breakpoints.
            </p>
            <a href="https://github.com/MrShahzaib005/code-flow" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link-inline font-mono" style="font-size: 0.75rem; margin-top: 0.75rem; display: inline-block;">
              View Repository →
            </a>
          </div>

          <div class="surface-card">
            <span class="mono-tag" style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Single Page Application</span>
            <h4>Dynamics 360 Event Explorer</h4>
            <p style="font-size: 0.875rem; margin-top: 0.35rem;">
              Zero-dependency JavaScript single-page application with asynchronous JSON parsing, real-time debounced filtering, and accessible modal navigation.
            </p>
            <a href="https://github.com/MrShahzaib005/dynamics360-featured-events" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link-inline font-mono" style="font-size: 0.75rem; margin-top: 0.75rem; display: inline-block;">
              View Repository →
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .lab-header {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
</style>
